algorithms.pseudocode:
MINIMAL-POLY-REAL-GENERATOR(n):
  Input: positive integer n >= 3
  Output: coefficients of minimal polynomial of 2cos(2pi/n) over Q

  roots <- empty list
  for k = 1 to n-1:
    if gcd(k, n) = 1:
      add 2*cos(2*pi*k/n) to roots (deduplicated)

  poly <- [1]  // start with constant polynomial 1
  for each root r in roots:
    poly <- poly * (X - r)  // expand product

  return round(poly coefficients to nearest integers)

Time: O(phi(n)^2)  Space: O(phi(n))
